# The 64-bit work of loft's own runtime in a 32-bit device image (@PLN217; `src/esp_width64.rs`).
# One line an exception: the function, or a prefix ending in `*`, then why it needs 64 bits.
# A line that allows nothing any more is reported in the build's report: remove it.
loft_log_clock          a log line's time is milliseconds since 1970, an i64
loft_push_decimal       prints an i64; a 32-bit value is printed by loft_format_int32
loft_format_long        prints an i64, and the 64 bits of a hex, octal or binary form
loft_sip_write          a keyed collection's digest is a 64-bit SipHash, the table's own format
loft_digest_str         the same digest, over a text key
loft_kv_cmp             compares a keyed collection's f64 key
loft_bt_record_part     compares an index's f64 key
loft_rx_word            a radix key is cut into 64-bit words, the tree's own format
loft_h_home             a table whose size is no power of two takes its bucket by a 64-bit remainder; a table loft sizes is a power of two and takes a mask
loft_h_ensure_table     a table's growth is sized in 64 bits so that it cannot wrap; once per growth
loft_h_inline_rebuild   the same, for a table held inline
loft_resize_store       a store's growth is sized in 64 bits so that it cannot wrap; once per growth
loft_heap_human         the heap-limit report writes a size with one decimal; printed when the limit is hit
